---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SourcePlate from "../../components/exhibits/SourcePlate.astro";
import ContributionExplorer from "../../components/exhibits/ContributionExplorer.astro";
export const prerender = false;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The source plate"
  description="A working exhibit: a contribution collected by one independently owned app, and the card composed from it by another. Separate the plates, change the source, hide it."
  path="/exhibits/source-plate/"
  currentPath="/exhibits/"
  image="/og/woodhouse-workshop-20261018.jpg"
>
  <section class="container exhibit-intro">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/exhibits/">Exhibits</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>The source plate</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="exhibit-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label">Working exhibit · App Composer</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">
          One photo.
          <br />
          <em>Two apps. One owner.</em>
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div class="exhibit-intro__aside">
        <p>
          Here / there collects photos. The owner approves them. Linkarooie features approved ones
          beside their own links. The second app does not own the photo, and it never keeps a copy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Below is the published Here / there contract, read through this site. Both sides of it are
          on screen. Change the source and the composed card changes with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container exhibit-stage">
    <SourcePlate />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <ContributionExplorer />
  </section>
  <section class="container exhibit-body">
    <div class="exhibit-body__grid">
      <div class="exhibit-prose">
        <h2>Why the second app has nothing of its own</h2>
        <p>
          A guestbook and a showcase could have been one app with two screens. They are not, and the
          difference is the whole point. They have separate repositories, separate deployments,
          separate storage and separate owners. The only thing that crosses between them is a
          versioned contract: a list of approved items, each with its own address, its own revision
          and its own visibility.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the showcase reads that contract rather than copying from it, one rule does the
          work. If the contribution is hidden or removed at the source, the feature disappears from
          the showcase on the next request. There is nothing to clean up in a second place, because
          there is no second copy.
        </p>
        <h2>What to take from it</h2>
        <p>If you are building a small system out of apps you already own:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Publish a contract, not a database.</strong> One versioned read model, with an
            item identifier, a revision and a visibility, is enough for a second app to compose
            from.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep the ownership honest.</strong> The feature is a reference, not a copy. The
            card leads back to the original contribution, and the original keeps its own address.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Let the source decide.</strong> Approval, hiding and removal happen in one
            place. Everything downstream reads the consequence.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Expect the honest limit.</strong> A photo that has already been downloaded
            cannot be recalled. The contract controls what the apps publish, not what a person has
            already kept.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="exhibit-prose__actions">
          <a class="home-action" href="https://composer.loftwah.com/demo">
            See the live pair <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/dispatches/your-apps-should-get-along/">
            Read the story behind it <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="exhibit-margin" aria-label="About this exhibit">
        <div class="exhibit-margin__block">
          <span class="micro-label">What you are looking at</span>
          <p>
            The published Here / there contract, read through this site’s own read-only route. The
            photo is served by the guestbook; the card beside it is composed here, from the same
            record.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="exhibit-margin__block">
          <span class="micro-label">What it does not claim</span>
          <p>
            The visibility switch changes the demonstration only. Nothing is sent to the guestbook,
            no contribution is hidden, and nothing is deleted. The postcards are labelled fictional
            demo material by the source app itself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="exhibit-margin__block">
          <span class="micro-label">Reviewed</span>
          <p>
            Source plate 20 October 2026. Contribution flow 23 October 2026. Contract version 1, as
            published by the guestbook.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .exhibit-intro {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .exhibit-intro__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem 4rem;
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .exhibit-intro .page-title {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .exhibit-intro__aside p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: 46ch;
    color: var(--copy);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .exhibit-stage {
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .exhibit-body {
    padding-block: 2.5rem 4rem;
  }
  .exhibit-body__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }
  .exhibit-prose h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font: 700 clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem)/1.15 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .exhibit-prose h2 + p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .exhibit-prose p {
    max-width: 66ch;
    color: var(--copy);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .exhibit-prose ul {
    max-width: 66ch;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--copy);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .exhibit-prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .exhibit-prose strong {
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .exhibit-prose__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .exhibit-margin {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .exhibit-margin__block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .exhibit-margin__block p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--copy-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .exhibit-intro__grid,
    .exhibit-body__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
